@startuml
title Catalog Management — Sequence Diagram
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
actor "Head Librarian" as L
boundary ":CatalogUI" as UI
control ":CatalogController" as C
database ":BookRepository" as DB
control ":AuditService" as A
note over L,A : Precondition: Head Librarian is signed in. Successful operations shown.
loop For each catalog management request
alt Add book
L -> UI : Enter new book details
UI -> C : save(bookDetails)
activate C
C -> DB : save(new active Book)
DB --> C : savedBook
else Edit book
L -> UI : Select book to edit
UI -> C : edit(bookId)
C -> DB : findById(bookId)
DB --> C : book
C --> UI : Display populated book form
L -> UI : Submit updated details
UI -> C : save(bookDetails)
C -> DB : findById(bookId)
DB --> C : existingBook
C -> DB : save(updated active Book)
DB --> C : savedBook
else Archive book
L -> UI : Confirm archive(bookId)
UI -> C : delete(bookId)
C -> DB : findById(bookId)
DB --> C : book
C -> C : setActive(false)
C -> DB : save(archived Book)
DB --> C : savedBook
end
C -> A : record(CREATE / UPDATE / ARCHIVE)
activate A
A --> C : completed
deactivate A
C --> UI : Redirect to /catalog + success message
deactivate C
UI --> L : Show refreshed catalog and confirmation
end
note over DB,A : Repository abstracts persistence. AuditService persists the audit log.
@enduml
